  "method": "Score all anatomies in six participants for each assumed lever offset. Pareto mode drops an anatomy only if a pilot anatomy has strictly lower losses in all six participants. Every resample has nonnegative weights summing to six, hence every discarded candidate has a strictly worse fit for every resample. Exhaustive mode retains all candidates. Both modes take exact weighted sums on a verified 2^-34 fixed-point lattice and resolve ties by smallest candidate ID. A runtime check verifies every participant loss converts exactly and every sum fits in the 53-bit significand of the CPU/H100 FP64 reference. All returned IDs were independently checked.",
